1809 0 obj
  << /ActualText (1\056 Background \050\176\3144\0142E\314FG\051\072\nOnline identitybased theft is one of the most serious and growing threats to individuals and organizations\056 Over the last 10 years\054 it has caused significant economic damage\056 The increasing availability of personal information on the Internet has amplified the chances of this cybercrime\056 Online identity theft results from a combination of cybercrimes and the lack of awareness and training regarding the protection of personal data\056\n2\056 Purpose \050G\057A\051\072\nThe aim of this research is to evaluate the need for a reformulation of the concept of identity theft\054 so that it is compatible with the evolution of behaviors and fraud tactics in the digital age\056\n3\056 Methodology \0501H4\0144F\0473\314\051\072\nThis paper provides a comprehensive explanation of online identity theft\054 examining the various approaches used by thieves to target individuals and organizations\054 as well as the types of fraud involved in this cybercrime\056\n4\056 Results \050F\052\047\314\054\051\072\nAlthough the specific results are not detailed in the provided text\054 it can be inferred that the paper explores different fraud techniques and provides a deeper understanding of how identity theft has evolved\056 This may include discussing various methods used by criminals and the broader impact of identity theft\056\n5\056 Conclusion \050F\052\314\054G\014\257\3141\314\051\072\nEducation and awareness are critical tools for consumers to protect themselves from online identity fraud\056 The research advocates for a redefinition of identity theft in line with the changing behaviors of fraudsters and technological advancements\056\n\nOnline identity theft\nCybercrime\nPersonal data protection\nAwareness and education\nIdentity fraud\nCybersecurity\nUser training\nEconomic damage\nFraud detection\n\n\n1\056 Background \050\176\3144\0142E\314FG\051\072\nAs billions of personal data is shared through social media and networks\054 data privacy and security have become a growing concern\056 Several efforts have been made to prevent identity information leakage from face photos using techniques such as image obfuscation\056 However\054 many of these methods are either perceptually unsatisfactory or ineffective against face recognition systems\056\n2\056 Purpose \050G\057A\051\072\nThe goal of this paper is to develop a technique that can encrypt personal photos to protect users from unauthorized face recognition systems while ensuring that the images remain visually identical to the original versions for human beings\056\n3\056 Methodology \0501H4\0144F\0473\314\051\072\nThe paper proposes a targeted identityprotection iterative method \050TIPIM\051 to generate adversarial identity masks that can be overlaid on facial images\056 These masks conceal the original identities without compromising the visual quality of the image\056\n4\056 Results \050F\052\047\314\054\051\072\nExtensive experiments show that TIPIM achieves a 951\045\053 protection success rate against various stateoftheart face recognition models under practical test scenarios\056 Additionally\054 the effectiveness of the method is demonstrated on a commercial API service\056\n5\056 Conclusion \050F\052\314\054G\014\257\3141\314\051\072\nTIPIM provides a highly effective solution for protecting identity in facial images from unauthorized recognition while maintaining visual fidelity\056 The method demonstrates strong applicability in realworld settings\054 ensuring both privacy and usability for users\056\n\nFace recognition\nData privacy\nImage obfuscation\nIdentity protection\nAdversarial masks\nVisual encryption\nTargeted identity protection\nFacial image security\nPrivacypreserving techniques\nFace recognition models\nCommercial API service)
