1813 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Abstract 1\072 Floor Monitoring System with Embedded Triboelectric Sensors\nBackground\072\nHighlights the significance of floor monitoring systems in smart homes for capturing sensory information from daily activities\056\nMentions the privacy advantage over camerabased systems and the limitations of triboelectric sensors \050humidity susceptibility\054 longterm stability\051\056\nPurpose \072\nTo develop a robust and reliable floor monitoring system addressing the limitations of triboelectric sensors\056\nMethodology\072\nIntegration of reliable triboelectric coding mats with deeplearningassisted data analytics\056\nUtilizes quaternary coding electrodes normalized to a reference electrode for stable detection\056\nImplements universal electrode patterns for costeffectiveness and simplicity\056\nExternal wiring allows distinctive coding for each floor mat and reduces system complexity\056\nResults\072\nAchieves a lowcost\054 largearea\054 and reliable floor monitoring system\056\nEnables position\057trajectory tracking\054 identity recognition\054 and automatic controls in smart home applications\056\nConclusion\072\nDemonstrates a significant advancement in floor sensing technology for smart homes with costeffective and reliable solutions\056\n\n\nAbstract 2\072 SelfSustainable Sensing Systems for Smart Homes\nBackground\072\nEmphasizes the role of selfsustainable sensing systems with micro\057nano sensors and nanoenergy harvesters in IoT systems\056\nNotes the importance of AIoT in enabling detection\054 analysis\054 and decisionmaking in smart homes\056\nPurpose \072\nTo review advances in micro\057nano sensors\054 energy harvesters\054 and their integration for selfsustainable IoT systems and smart homes\056\nTo explore future directions in healthcare and wearable sensing systems enabled by AIoT\056\nMethodology\072\nDiscusses conventional and wearable micro\057nano sensors and energy harvesters\056\nPresents integration approaches for selfsustainable IoT systems\056\nReviews advancements in AIoT systems and machinelearningenabled smart home applications\056\nResults\072\nProvides insights into selfsustainable sensing platforms for IoT systems\056\nHighlights applications such as smart home healthcare and wearable sensing systems\056\nConclusion\072\nIdentifies future directions\054 including bioelectronic medicine and wearable photonics sensing systems\054 as key advancements for smart homes\056)
